\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces 21D geometric dataset analysis. \textbf  {Top-left}: KS heatmap for all 13 geometric features across 4 pairs. All values are below 0.04; \textit  {surf\_variation} and \textit  {dist\_centroid} are the strongest individual discriminators. \textbf  {Top-right}: mean Moran's~I per feature. Distance features have near-perfect autocorrelation ($I > 0.97$), while Laplacian curvature and planarity are more locally variable. \textbf  {Bottom-left}: SW comparison shows SW(13D geom) $\leq $ 0.041 for all pairs. \textbf  {Bottom-right}: SVM balanced accuracy --- adding geometric features gives $+$0.085 for the hardest pair (61,\,90) and $+$0.062 for (86,\,14), suggesting geometric shape provides complementary information to electrostatics.}}{14}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:geom}{{8}{14}{21D geometric dataset analysis. \textbf {Top-left}: KS heatmap for all 13 geometric features across 4 pairs. All values are below 0.04; \textit {surf\_variation} and \textit {dist\_centroid} are the strongest individual discriminators. \textbf {Top-right}: mean Moran's~I per feature. Distance features have near-perfect autocorrelation ($I > 0.97$), while Laplacian curvature and planarity are more locally variable. \textbf {Bottom-left}: SW comparison shows SW(13D geom) $\leq $ 0.041 for all pairs. \textbf {Bottom-right}: SVM balanced accuracy --- adding geometric features gives $+$0.085 for the hardest pair (61,\,90) and $+$0.062 for (86,\,14), suggesting geometric shape provides complementary information to electrostatics}{figure.caption.24}{}}
